    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d249">

                <pb facs="0314" n="302" sameAs="frus:frus1941v02/pg302"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/10190: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Algiers</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Cole</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Algiers</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-04-22T15:00:00+01:00">April 22, 1941—3
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 22—2:48 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>158. Your 91, April 18.<anchor n="24" xml:id="d249-f1"/> Message conveyed as
                    instructed. Chatel’s<anchor n="24a" xml:id="d249-f2"/> reaction: Warning
                    strengthens Marshal’s hands as well as Weygand’s. Vichy informed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cole</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d249-f1" n="24" xml:id="d249-f1-content">
                <p>See footnote 19, <ref target="#pg292">p. 292</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d249-f2" n="24a" xml:id="d249-f2-content">
                <p>Yves Chatel, Secretary General of the Delegation General in French Africa.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
